Q: CodeIgniter Convert Array to Json A: <p>I think you should put <code>echo</code> instead of <code>return</code> on Api2 Controller</p>
<pre><code>public function index()
{
    header('Content-Type: Application/json');
    $values['data'] = $this-&gt;Book_model-&gt;get_all_books();

    echo json_encode($values['data']);
}
</code></pre>
<p>or you can use build-in function <code>output</code> from CodeIgniter</p>
<pre><code>public function index()
{
    $values['data'] = $this-&gt;Book_model-&gt;get_all_books();

    $this-&gt;output
         -&gt;set_content_type('application/json', 'utf8')
         -&gt;set_output( json_encode($values['data']) );
}
</code></pre>

Q: Can&#39;t use properties and methods from the object passed as an argument to the Phaser event handler function A: <p>The issue is that you are using the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Spread_syntax" rel="nofollow noreferrer">spread operator</a> on a parameter, that is not needed.</p>
<p>Just remove it in this line and it should work:</p>
<pre><code>const testEventListener = (args: any[]) =&gt; {
    // ...
};
</code></pre>

Q: GetIsNetworkAvailable() behaves differently depending on .NET version A: <p>Let me talk about the reason first. This <a href="https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/100824" rel="nofollow noreferrer">PR</a> resulted in the return of some NDIS interfaces by the <code>NetworkInterface.GetAllNetworkInterfaces</code> method, some of them are not actually connected, but their OperationalStatus is always Up.</p>
<p>So this is only a problem on Windows, I can think 5 ways to solve it:</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Use the Windows API <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/iphlpapi/nf-iphlpapi-getadaptersaddresses" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>GetAdaptersAddresses</code></a>, but do not pass the <code>GAA_FLAG_INCLUDE_ALL_INTERFACES</code> flag, in order to get the same result as .NET8.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Further filtering of the existing results returned by <code>GetAllNetworkInterfaces</code>. You can check whether the interface has ipv4 support, a physical address, gateway, or unicast address:</p>
<pre><code>bool isNetworkReallyAvailable = NetworkInterface
     .GetAllNetworkInterfaces()
     .Any(ni =&gt;
          ni.OperationalStatus == OperationalStatus.Up &amp;&amp;
          ni.NetworkInterfaceType != NetworkInterfaceType.Loopback &amp;&amp;
          ni.NetworkInterfaceType != NetworkInterfaceType.Tunnel &amp;&amp;
          // Choose one
          ni.Supports(NetworkInterfaceComponent.IPv4) &amp;&amp;
          ni.GetPhysicalAddress().Equals(PhysicalAddress.None) &amp;&amp;
          ni.GetIPProperties().GatewayAddresses.Count &gt; 0 &amp;&amp;
          ni.GetIPProperties().UnicastAddresses.Count &gt; 0
     );
</code></pre>
</li>
<li><p>You can remove those interfaces: <a href="https://superuser.com/questions/1257859/remove-an-unused-hidden-network-connection-so-that-an-existing-name-can-be-reuse">https://superuser.com/questions/1257859/remove-an-unused-hidden-network-connection-so-that-an-existing-name-can-be-reuse</a></p>
</li>
<li><p>Go back to .NET8, fire an issue on github, and wait for a later version to fix it.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Consider using other methods, such as <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/13625304/check-internet-connection-availability-in-windows-8">this</a>, <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2031824/what-is-the-best-way-to-check-for-internet-connectivity-using-net">this</a>, and <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/20309158/c-sharp-checking-internet-connection">this</a>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
